<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Hawley Glover</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1829–1885</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Hawley Glover was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> officer and colonial administrator who served as administrator of the British colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lagos">Lagos</a> for most of the years from 1863 to 1872. He extended British influence into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> hinterland and raised an armed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> police force, the forerunner of the Nigerian army. He later led a column in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-ashanti-wars">Anglo-Ashanti War</a> of 1873–74 and was twice Governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-hawley-glover.jpg" alt="John Hawley Glover" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_John_Hawley_Glover_(1829-1885).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
